---
description: Keep each research paper in its own project under papers/
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is the home for research-paper reading. The `papers/` directory is the only place those projects go.

- Create each paper as its own directory: `papers/<slug>/`.
- Keep notes, questions, and the summary for that paper inside its directory.
- Add a paper with `python3 tools/paper.py new "Title" --url "https://..." --website "the site"`.
- After the source link or title changes in `paper.json`, run `python3 tools/paper.py index`.
- Record the link and write the student's own notes. Leave the paper's full text on the source site.
